    "mathematical_result_valid": true,
    "exact_theorem": "For a>b>0,0<lambda<b^2, fix the outer ellipse and proper confocal elliptical caustic. If the physical family has least N divisible by four, its signed original-trajectory area times signed area of perpendicular feet of each fixed finite real M on the original complete side lines is phase independent. All admitted coprime primitive stars and both traversal orientations; zero or negative pedal areas allowed.",
    "publication_form": "Attributed alternative incidence-curve proof research note",
    "exact_contemporary_overlap": "Alper Ferudun, Pedal Areas of Periodic Elliptic Billiard Trajectories with Respect to an Arbitrary Point, v1.0,15October2026, DOI10.5281/zenodo.23400541, TheoremA: the same theorem, with stronger complex-M allowance; also radial dependence, four-period value and repeated-orbit caveat. Section4 uses complementary poles and reversal zeros; the example here is a rescaling of his Table2.",
    "source_contract": "Reznik-Garcia-Koiller journal DOI10.1007/s40598-021-00174-y Section3.3/Table3p346 and arxiv2004.12497v11 Table3p6 give k203,a as signed original-side pedal product,allM,N0mod4. They do not literally print primitive or least period. This note imposes that necessary explicit interpretation; doubling primitive-six trajectories gives a nominal12-entry counterexample to the unrestricted interpretation. The historic question mark is not a current-openness certificate.",
    "timeline_limits": "The currently public original PR203 record gives server creation2026-10-01T05:24:27Z and original HEAD8edca9d773c085adb4ed0611357a7a2957e3395d contains the preserved proof. Ferudun record23400541 was created2026-10-15T16:11:42.588744Z and DataCite registered16:11:43Z. These are verified object-record dates, not authenticated discovery times, historical visibility at every instant, earliest disclosure or certified independent discovery. Separate contemporary records; no firstness claim. The current manuscript and later audits are dated16October2026, not backdated.",
    "method_credit_and_limits": "This is an attributed incidence-curve presentation using explicit branch charts and complementary pole/zero cancellation. Established Poncelet flag curves/involutions/meromorphic methods are credited to Schwartz-Tabachnikov, AST and Chavez-Caliz; Steiner radiality and the Bialy-Tabachnikov earlier four-period implication are credited. Neither theorem nor proof method is claimed novel. The published proof does not require the original Jacobi/contact-trace route or the separate credited AA-prime theorem; those original inputs were independently audited and are preserved as provenance.",
